# Build-context ALLOW-LIST for deploy/docker/backup.Dockerfile ONLY.
#
# BuildKit uses this file instead of the root .dockerignore whenever the
# build targets deploy/docker/backup.Dockerfile specifically (`<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore`
# convention). The root .dockerignore intentionally excludes scripts/ and
# docs/ for the production gateway image (Dockerfile) — this image is the
# one exception that actually needs them, so it gets its own list rather
# than weakening the root one.
#
# this file used to be a DENY-list whose patterns (no `**/` prefix) matched only at
# the context root — the defect fixed for the root .dockerignore. Present in the working tree and NOT excluded:
# `.stryker-tmp-*/sandbox-*/` (copies of .env, .env.prod, .scratch-f16/{collector-key.pem,kek.txt,ops-token.txt},
# data/keys.json, data/signing-identities.json …) and quarantine/**/{keys,signing-identities}.json. deploy/docker/backup.Dockerfile's
# `COPY . .` put them in an image layer, and its later `RUN rm -rf` could not remove anything from that earlier layer.
#
# Rule (same as the root .dockerignore): EVERYTHING is excluded; only the inputs this image runs are re-included,
# and nested test/secret material is excluded again at ANY depth afterwards. Adding a file to the image means adding
# it here deliberately. Inputs, derived from the runtime require() closure of scripts/dr/*.js and
# scripts/dr/probes/*.js (166 files, all under src/, services/ and scripts/dr/ — re-derived for this change) plus
# the shell entry points the CronJobs / systemd units run. deploy/docker/backup.Dockerfile's build-time content gate fails the
# build if a key, certificate, keystore or env file still reaches /app.

*

# ── Runtime sources ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!src/**
!services/**
# reached through the require() closure (src/core/dlp/extensionPoint.js -> enterprise/dlp); the backup never runs DLP but its dependency walk must resolve
!enterprise/**
!scripts/pg-backup.sh
!scripts/pg-wal-archive.sh
!scripts/backup-audit-log.sh
# the incremental audit-log backup's byte-range / metadata-chain helper (required by backup-audit-log.sh)
!scripts/audit-log-backup-chain.js
!scripts/dr/**
# docs/ is kept (runbooks referenced by the backup scripts' operator messages — see deploy/docker/backup.Dockerfile header)
!docs/**
!LICENSE
!licenses/THIRD-PARTY.md

# ── Excluded again at ANY depth, whatever was re-included above ─────────────────
**/__tests__/**
enterprise/dlp/eval/**
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js
**/test-fixtures/**
**/node_modules/**
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.crt
**/keys.json
**/*-keys.json
**/mac-keys*.json
**/signing-identities.json
**/*.log
**/*.sqlite
**/.DS_Store
